{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121153","id":4026690650,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7wAmxa","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121153","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121153.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121153.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121153","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121153/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121153/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121153/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/32c6c0b181bfbd85e4a081c78758ce57064218ea","number":121153,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Add the ability to disable/enable playing in the Editor","user":{"login":"Komariarii","id":301026105,"node_id":"U_kgDOEfFLOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/301026105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii","html_url":"https://github.com/Komariarii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Komariarii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds the ability to (ideally temporarily) disable all conventional methods of playing through the editor. This mostly means the Play button, Current Scene button, and Custom Scene button. Which includes their hotkeys.\r\n\r\nThis is called via `EditorInterface.playing_enabled`. (Naming is admittedly not the best, but I couldn't think of anything better)\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\nThis PR does nothing by itself, it's a prerequisite for #121156, it still does have some uses by itself though. Such as..\r\n\r\nEnabling plugins to have better UX, if you have a process that _needs_ to run prior to the user starting their game this will help prevent that. \r\nAn example would be a plugin that downloads some arbitrary data or creates some arbitrary data (such as a json file containing game data), that may take longer than a single frame would benefit from temporarily disabling playing, as to make sure the user does not accidentally corrupt/break their game with no discernible cause. \r\n\r\nThis also disables \"Reload\" functionality, as it's assumed if playing is disabled, reloading wouldn't be desirable either. (In the case of #121156 for instance)\r\n\r\nA video example of \"play\" toggling\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52fd1f8c-dd42-47d3-beca-5b34b193d58e\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/mile